It also uses React's `useState` and `useEffect` hooks, as well as the `useField` hook from the `formik` library to handle form input fields.

When the user starts typing in the input field, a dropdown menu appears showing all possible options of the input, and the items in the dropdown menu change depending on the typed user value. If the value doesn't exist, the dropdown menu disappears.

If the input is invalid, the input field has a red border.

The component is fully optimized for a large amount of options in the dropdown menu. It uses the `useMemo` hook to memoize the options dropdown, preventing unnecessary re-renders.

